        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Should now be part of the latest `main` after a last minute tweak: `pattern and #pattern > 0 and pattern or nil` -> `if type(pattern) == 'table' and #pattern == 0 then pattern = nil end`. Mostly because I fell that Lua's hack for a \"ternary operator\" works clearly only if it is `aaa and xxx or yyy`. If the condition requires extra subconditions (`aaa and bbb and xxx or yyy`), then it is very confusing to me.",
